WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.739
How do we get our customers and

00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:03.729
suppliers to buy into

00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:05.270
our WHY?

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.939
To buy into our -

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:09.780
How to - how do I get somebody that

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.200
I went on a date with to fall in

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.530
love with me?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.480
It's like.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.970
You you're asking the wrong

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.259
question.

00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:20.630
You have to be clear

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.060
and open about what you stand for.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.420
And just like when you hire

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.079
somebody, you want

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:28.089
to make sure that when you hire

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:30.300
them, that they share your values,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.420
that they believe in your vision.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.420
You know, they don't just think it's

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.290
corny, you know, or

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.470
marketing, but rather

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.380
that they buy into it.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.320
And sometimes we'll make mistakes.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.880
And sometimes people will come and

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.250
they fall in love with it after the

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.250
fact.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.250
But it's, you know, we try on

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.290
balance to bring people that we

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.440
believe will get along

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.440
with the people who work here

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.770
because of our values and our cause.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.270
And so too, is it with with

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.940
suppliers.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.920
I think that

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.730
or clients are it's

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:01.940
the same thing, which is we stand

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.780
for what we stand for and our goal

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.059
is to attract people who believe

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:06.460
what we believe.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.030
The more vocal we are about

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.259
what we believe those people

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:11.210
literally will come to us

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.400
or turn down a competitor,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.280
who may even be cheaper, because

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.960
they would rather do business with

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:17.960
us.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.219
And so it's OK

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:21.189
to do business with a supplier that

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:22.880
doesn't believe what we believe, but

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.770
we have to go in with eyes open

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.069
knowing full well that this is just

00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:27.439
a transaction.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.570
You offer a decent product.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:29.780
You give me a decent price.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:30.859
This is not going to be a lifelong

00:01:30.859 --> 00:01:31.859
relationship.

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:32.859
This is a

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.479
transactional relationship.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:36.030
And when it's done, I'm

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.030
just going to hold you to very

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.030
different

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.030
standards, right?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.030
Because when it's transactional,

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.030
we're a little less patient when

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.039
things go wrong

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:45.289
and sometimes we you just can't do

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:46.289
that too often.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:47.289
It's like if you're

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:48.420
living a healthy lifestyle, you can

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.100
have chocolate cake and just not too

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.100
often.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.229
So, yeah, I think the more vocal you

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:54.700
are, the more you attract and then

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.700
you have to make decisions like

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.700
you're hiring people because they're

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.920
going to become a member of your

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:58.920
family as well.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.920
This is the

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.189
difference between

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:03.259
the short-term, finite minded

00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:05.829
and the long-term infinite minded,

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:07.670
the finite-minded.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.129
Is it the cheapest today?

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.360
Is it the best relationship today?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.500
And pay no attention to the

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.769
secondary or tertiary effects

00:02:14.769 --> 00:02:16.939
and definitely pay no attention to

00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:18.850
what will happen in five years.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.780
Whereas that long-term minded,

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.450
infinite-minded player

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.560
looks at its looks

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.540
at something and looks at someone

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.260
and says, "Well, you know you're not

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.159
the cheapest, but I think we're

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:34.209
going to get along just fine."

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:36.129
And over the course of time,

00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:37.829
the quality of work will

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:39.350
far outweigh whatever you paid.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.129
A friend of mine who's a consultant

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:43.379
loves to joke about her clients

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:44.960
that they never have the time or

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.599
money to do it right the first time,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.879
but they always have the time and

00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:50.420
money to do it again.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.629
And I think when you're

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:52.629
infinite-minded, you consider those

00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:53.719
factors from the from the beginning.

